{"step_index":131,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:39:53Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:39:53+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:39:53+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/pipeline/lean_disproof.py`\nTotal Lines: 291\nTotal Bytes: 13556\nShowing lines 150 to 220\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n150: \n151: \n152: def _parse(statement: str, columns) -> Optional[Tuple[List[str], str]]:\n153:     \"\"\"(classes, lean_body) for a class-conditioned inequality.\n154: \n155:     The body is any rational linear comparison, not just ``invariant REL\n156:     invariant``. Restricting it to bare invariants rejected most of what the\n157:     generator actually produces — constant bounds like ``zero_forcing_number ≤\n158:     8`` and scaled forms like ``maximum_degree ≤ 2 · independence_number`` — so\n159:     conjectures went unrefuted for want of a parser rather than for want of a\n160:     counterexample.\n161: \n162:     ``linear_form`` does the rewriting, the same module the necessary-condition\n163:     branch uses. It scales by the lcm of the denominators and moves negative\n164:     terms across, so every coefficient ends up non-negative and the ℕ statement\n165:     is equivalent rather than merely truncated.\n166:     \"\"\"\n167:     if \"⇒\" not in statement:\n168:         return None\n169:     cond, body = statement.split(\"⇒\", 1)\n170:     classes = [c for c in columns if re.search(r\"\\b\" + re.escape(c) + r\"\\b\", cond)]\n171:     if not classes or any(c not in CLASS_PREDICATES for c in classes):\n172:         return None\n173:     # A body that is itself all classes is the necessary-condition shape.\n174:     names = set(linear_form.invariants(body))\n175:     if not names or names <= set(CLASS_PREDICATES):\n176:         return None\n177:     if any(n not in SUPPORTED for n in names):\n178:         return None\n179:     rendered = linear_form.render_comparison(b\n<truncated 205 bytes>\nnt: str) -> Optional[Tuple[str, str]]:\n186:     \"\"\"(lean_hypothesis, lean_conclusion) for an ``(inequality) ⇒ classes``\n187:     survivor, else None.\n188: \n189:     The hypothesis is normalised to ℕ by ``linear_form`` — the same rewriting the\n190:     positive exporter applies, so the theorem and its disproof are statements\n191:     about the same proposition.\n192:     \"\"\"\n193:     if \"⇒\" not in statement:\n194:         return None\n195:     cond, concl = statement.split(\"⇒\", 1)\n196:     clauses = linear_form.parse_class_conclusion(concl)\n197:     if not clauses or any(c not in CLASS_PREDICATES for _, c in clauses):\n198:         return None\n199:     names = set(linear_form.invariants(cond))\n200:     if not names or names <= set(CLASS_PREDICATES):\n201:         return None                        # class-conditioned shape, not this one\n202:     if any(n not in SUPPORTED for n in names):\n203:         return None\n204:     hyp = linear_form.render_comparison(cond, SUPPORTED)\n205:     if hyp is None:\n206:         return None\n207:     goal = \" ∧ \".join(\n208:         f\"¬ {CLASS_PREDICATES[c]} G\" if neg else f\"{CLASS_PREDICATES[c]} G\"\n209:         for neg, c in clauses)\n210:     # Mirror the theorem: the conjecture is about non-trivial graphs, so a\n211:     # disproof must exhibit one. Omitting this made every statement of this\n212:     # shape refutable by Fin 0, where the class predicates hold vacuously.\n213:     guards = [f\"{CLASS_PREDICATES['nontrivial']} G\"] + \\\n214:         definedness_hyps(names, lambda h: f\"GraphCalc.{h} G\")\n215:     return \" → \".join(guards + [hyp]), goal\n216: \n217: \n218: def is_supported(statement: str, columns, witness_graph6: Optional[str]) -> bool:\n219:     \"\"\"True iff